                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "52a25b24-c1bc-3db8-bfe9-72378d36a7ed",
                        "entry_id": "1fe7606e-39d5-31ec-a91a-cdb08df4bbbf",
                        "glosses": [
                            "to hold, to hold back"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "fc7c9c46-ade7-443d-9b3c-fb0d8c203954",
                                "sense_id": "52a25b24-c1bc-3db8-bfe9-72378d36a7ed",
                                "text": "Наконе́ц бри́чка, сде́лавши поря́дочный скачо́к, опусти́лась, как бу́дто в я́му, в воро́та гости́ницы, и Чи́чиков был встре́чен Петру́шкою, кото́рый одно́ю руко́ю приде́рживал полу́ своего́ сюртука́, и́бо не люби́л, что́бы расходи́лись по́лы, а друго́ю стал помога́ть ему́ вылеза́ть из бри́чки.",
                                "translation": "At last the chaise with a violent jolt seemed to drop into a hole, as it passed in at the gates of the hotel, and Tchitchikov was met by Petrushka, who with one hand held the skirts of his coat, for he could not bear them to fly apart, and with the other began helping his master out of the chaise.",
                                "english": "At last the chaise with a violent jolt seemed to drop into a hole, as it passed in at the gates of the hotel, and Tchitchikov was met by Petrushka, who with one hand held the skirts of his coat, for he could not bear them to fly apart, and with the other began helping his master out of the chaise."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
